C o m p i l a t i o n


      CEE 6410 - Engineering Systems Analysis
      Homework 3 - Network Shipping Problem
       
      THE PROBLEM:
       
      An automobile company must decide how to move cars from suppliers in Kansas City
        and Dallas to dealerships in New York, Minneapolis, Seattle, and San Francisco.
       
      Suppliers or Dealerships     Kansas City (KC)     Dallas (DAL)
      New York (NY)                $12/car              $15/car       250 car
      Minneapolis (MIN)            $4/car               $9/car        400 car
      Seattle (SEA)                $18/car              $21/car       450 car
      San Francisco (SF)           $18/car              $17/car       450 car
      Vehicles/supplier            1000                 800
       
      Determine the optimal shipping volumes to move cars between the locations.
       
      THE SOLUTION:
      Uses General Algebraic Modeling System to Solve this Linear Program
       
      Created:
      Samuel T. Torgersen-Gonzalez
      s.torgersen-gonzalez@usu.edu
      September 27, 2026
  27   
  28  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
  29  SETS sup cars at suppliers /KC, DAL/
  30       deal dealerships /NY, MIN, SEA, SF/;
  31   
  32  * 2. DEFINE input data
  33  PARAMETERS
  34     c(sup) Objective function coefficients (cars per supplier)
  35           /KC  1000,
  36            DAL  800/
  37   
  38     b(deal) Right hand constraint values (number of sales at each dealership)
  39           /NY   250,
  40            MIN  400,
  41            SEA  450,
  42            SF   450/;
  43   
  44  TABLE A(sup,deal) Left hand side constraint coefficients
  45          NY   MIN    SEA   SF
  46  KC      12    4     18    18
  47  DAL     15    9     21    17;
  48   
  49   
  50  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  51  VARIABLES X(sup,deal) cars to be shipped from supplier to dealership (Number)
  52            VCOST  total shipping cost ($);
  53   
  54  * Non-negativity constraints
  55  POSITIVE VARIABLES X;
  56   
  57  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  58  EQUATIONS
  59     COST Total cost ($) and objective function value
  60     SUPPLY_CONSTRAIN(sup) Supplier supply
  61     DEAL_CONSTRAIN(deal) Dealership orders;
  62   
  63  COST..                    VCOST =E= SUM((sup,deal), A(sup,deal)*X(sup,deal));
  64  SUPPLY_CONSTRAIN(sup)..   SUM(deal, X(sup,deal)) =L= c(sup);
  65  DEAL_CONSTRAIN(deal)..    SUM(sup, X(sup,deal)) =G= b(deal);
  66   
  67   
  68  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
  69  MODEL SHIPPING /COST, SUPPLY_CONSTRAIN, DEAL_CONSTRAIN/;
  70  *Altnerative way to write (include all previously defined equations)
  71  *MODEL PRODUCTING /ALL/;
  72   
  73   
  74  * 6. SOLVE the MODEL
  75  * Solve the PRODUCTING model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  76  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  77  SOLVE SHIPPING USING LP MINIMIZING VCOST;
  78   
  79   
  80  * 6. CLick File menu => RUN (F9) or Solve icon and examine solution report in .LST file


